# DZQL Framework - Concise AI Guide

## Language: Plain JavaScript only (NO TypeScript)

## What is DZQL?
PostgreSQL framework with automatic CRUD via WebSocket RPC. Every entity gets 5 operations: GET, SAVE, DELETE, LOOKUP, SEARCH.

## Core API Pattern
```javascript
// All operations via: ws.api.{operation}.{entity}(params)
const venue = await ws.api.get.venues({id: 1});           // Single record
const saved = await ws.api.save.venues({name: 'MSG'});    // Upsert
const deleted = await ws.api.delete.venues({id: 1});      // Delete
const options = await ws.api.lookup.venues({p_filter: 'msg'}); // Autocomplete
const results = await ws.api.search.venues({filters: {city: 'NYC'}}); // Paginated
```

## Entity Registration (Required for features)
```sql
SELECT dzql.register_entity(
  p_table_name := 'venues',
  p_label_field := 'name',
  p_searchable_fields := array['name', 'address'],
  p_fk_includes := '{"org": "organisations", "sites": "sites"}'::jsonb,
  p_graph_rules := '{
    "on_create": {
      "rule_name": {
        "actions": [{"type": "create", "entity": "table", "data": {"field": "@value"}}]
      }
    }
  }'::jsonb
);
```

## Graph Rules Variables
- `@user_id`, `@id`, `@field_name`, `@now`, `@today`

## Path Syntax (permissions/notifications)
- `@field` - field value
- `->table[condition]{active}.field` - traverse relationships
- `$` in conditions = current field value

## Authentication
```javascript
await ws.call('login_user', {email: 'user@email.com', password: 'pass'});
// All subsequent operations auto-include user_id
```

## Custom Functions
PostgreSQL: First param MUST be `p_user_id INT`
Bun: First param MUST be `userId`
Call via: `ws.call('funcName', params)`

## Database Structure
- Core: `packages/dzql/src/database/migrations/001-007*.sql`
- Domain: `packages/{app}/database/init_db/008+*.sql`

## Testing Commands
```bash
bun venues:db && sleep 5 && bun venues:test  # Reset DB + test
bun venues:logs                               # View logs
```

## Key Points
- FK includes: `{"field": "table"}` for dereferencing OR collections
- Graph rules execute on data changes automatically
- Deleted records throw "record not found" errors (don't return empty objects)
- Use temporal `{active}` filtering in paths
- Reset database between test runs for isolation
